# Stripe/Linear SaaS UI/UX Excellence Rule

When generating, modifying, or refactoring UI components and pages in this repository, you **MUST** follow Stripe/Linear SaaS design standards:

## 1. Zero Basic / Conventional Web Design
- Do NOT create generic white background websites with basic blue buttons or wall-of-text service cards.
- Always use **Obsidian/Slate Dark Mode (`#030712`, `#0B0F19`, `#0F172A`)** with subtle glass borders (`1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08)`).
- Pair dark obsidian surfaces with **Warm Imperial Gold (`#D4AF37`)** for institutional CTAs and subtle **Cyan (`#06B6D4`)** or **Emerald (`#10B981`)** for financial calculation metrics.

## 2. Bento Grid Modular Architecture
- Structure feature catalogs, service lists, and dashboard metrics into modular **Bento Grid cells** (`grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4`).
- Use spotlight hover glows (`hover:border-gold-500/40 hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(212,175,55,0.15)]`) on all bento cards.

## 3. Product-Led Above-The-Fold Utility
- The homepage Hero section MUST include an **interactive product widget** (e.g., live RoDTEP/EPCG Duty Calculator or Consultation Slot Booker) above the fold.
- Never use generic hero illustrations or stock imagery placeholders.

## 4. Craftsmanship & Micro-Interactions
- Use smooth hover translations (`hover:-translate-y-1`), scale feedback (`active:scale-95`), and animated status badges (`animate-pulse`).
- All code MUST be clean, production-grade, and free of AI comments or AI code smells.
